  "section_notes": "The final S2 sets an 8% permanent ceiling with no sales stop between 5% and 8%, existing models are not exempt, and per-model rates go to regulators and purchasers but not the public, which favours Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S3 gives an open 'where feasible' retrofit escape with a six-year minimum deadline, also favouring Northwind (38% shut-off coverage). S5 makes recall mandatory above 8 per 100k with no interim window, which constrains Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9), while S4's 36-month suppression start favours Halcyon."
